{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"defeasible-fretful-pekingese","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nBug b594-de6d-3ebc-490f fixed reroute_migrated_plans so inbound update, conflict and repair_property plans are no longer dispatched through the outbound handlers. The selection filter was unchanged from 2026-08-25 (d49466b5e96), so bridge runs since then may have written Jira-side changes back to Jira or reposted Jira comments. No production run has been inspected.\n\n## Approach\nRead-only: sample bridge-run manifests and Jira issue histories since 2026-08-25 for an update_issue or add_comment on a key whose same-pass plan was inbound, and for comment duplicates. Record issue keys and comment ids on this ticket. Do not write to Jira.\n\n## Testing\nRead-only inspection of recorded manifests and Jira history; no code change.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A sample of bridge-run manifests since 2026-08-25 is checked for outbound writes against inbound plans (checked: result and the sampled run ids recorded in a ticket comment).\n- [ ] Any duplicated Jira comment or written-back field found is listed with issue key and comment id, or the sample is recorded as clean.\n","id":"ff27-ebf3-236d-437f","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["reconciler","ops","verification"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Check whether past bridge runs wrote inbound Jira changes back to Jira"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792827820125444001,"uuid":"bb5446ec-5456-42c5-89f6-d9a0e7a9915d"}